ng away worse hands.\n\nReason:  \nYou have a near-nut hand. The only losing scenario is if opponent holds **6♠6♥** (only combo for better full house). Any other holding they have is either equal (split) or worse. Since they checked the river, they likely don’t have the absolute nuts. A small **value bet** (like 100) can extract chips from weaker made hands (e.g., 6x, 3x, or bluffs). Given your chip lead and game context (you're ahead overall), maximizing expected value without overcommitting is ideal. A minimal raise balances risk and reward.\n\nAnswer: 100"}
